        "original_id": "10d9b193-8ef3-5561-ad25-9ae19bb65afb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701\n- Places: Little Rock, Arkansas; Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport; Hennepin County, Minnesota; Minneapolis; Saint Paul; Upper Midwest region\n- Organizations: Pinnacle Airlines\n\nFacts:\n- Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701 was an overnight repositioning flight with no passengers from Little Rock, Arkansas, to Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport.\n- Both crew members on Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701 were killed.\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is located in a portion of Hennepin County, Minnesota, outside of any city or school district.\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is within 10 miles of both downtown Minneapolis and downtown Saint Paul.\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is the largest and busiest airport in the six-state Upper Midwest region of Minnesota, Iowa, Nebraska, North Dakota, South Dakota, and Wisconsin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
